        {
            "number": 5,
            "revision": "160686d6ab4b7a0389c49886ad90303a75f9fe23",
            "parents": [
                "4b77934919ba054450db2a9a5de4ab2392ab32fc"
            ],
            "ref": "refs/changes/97/79297/5",
            "uploader": {
                "name": "Alexander",
                "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                "username": "pointbazaar"
            },
            "createdOn": 1743517024,
            "author": {
                "name": "Alexander",
                "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                "username": "pointbazaar"
            },
            "kind": "TRIVIAL_REBASE",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "schemas/legacy.json",
                    "line": 488,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "The design with the physical topology entries is that a board could have all sorts of different ports on it, like PS port, riser port, BMC card port, etc.\n\n(docs are: https://github.com/openbmc/entity-manager/blob/master/docs/associations.md,  https://github.com/openbmc/docs/blob/master/designs/physical-topology.md).\n\nSo far it's hardly used though, people may not be interested in all the associations needed for Redfish yet.\n\nthe code at https://github.com/openbmc/entity-manager/blob/master/src/topology.cpp#L38 just needs the upstream side to end in 'Port', so maybe this can be an enum with just 1 entry now?  Does that conflict with the the enumerating of the Type field in your other commit?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "schemas/legacy.json",
                    "line": 488,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Thanks for pointing out the relevant design \ud83d\ude0a\n\nI was mostly going off of the existing configurations when creating this series,\nso this is a good opportunity for people to come in and refine each schema with the relevant background and experience.\n\n> just needs the upstream side to end in 'Port', so maybe this can be an enum with just 1 entry now? Does that conflict with the the enumerating of the Type field in your other commit?\n\nIt should not conflict since no other value for ```Type``` ends in \"Port\",\nfrom what's been enumerated.\n\nTechnically, my commit for enumerating ```Type``` field is not fully complete when considering the design wording ```The upstream port has a type ending in Port (such as a BackplanePort, PowerInputPort, etc)``` since some possibilities from the design are not covered. I still would prefer to keep that patch as is since the intent there was to enumerate what's in the upstream configs.\n\n> so maybe this can be an enum with just 1 entry now?  \n\nSure \ud83d\udc4d.\nI will also create ```description``` property pointing to the design, so folks know that the enum may be extended."
                },
                {
                    "file": "schemas/legacy.json",
                    "line": 511,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "This should be optional, as not every port is a power port."
                },
                {
                    "file": "schemas/legacy.json",
                    "line": 511,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                }
            ],
